\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every fixed $\beta >1$ in Gaussian SK, is there $c_\beta >0$ independent of n and realized disorder such that a Gibbs-sampled initial configuration has mixing time at most $\exp (n^{1-c_\beta })$, with joint probability tending to one?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every fixed $\beta >1$ in Gaussian SK, is there $c_\beta >0$ independent of n and realized disorder such that a Gibbs-sampled initial configuration has mixing time at most $\exp (n^{1-c_\beta })$, with joint probability tending to one?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-typical-start-upper-bound-for-low-temperature-SK-Glauber-dynamics-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex}.
